    <string name="help_player_title">In a video</string>
    <string name="help_shorts_title">In the shorts feed</string>
    <string name="help_library_title">In the library</string>

    <string name="help_player_body">Tap to show the controls; tap again to put them away.\n\nDrag up and down on the left for brightness, on the right for volume. Volume carries on past 100%% into amplification, marked in amber.\n\nDrag sideways to scrub. Nothing moves until you let go, so you can change your mind.\n\nDrag down from the top to close.\n\nDouble tap the left or right side to jump ten seconds.\n\nPress and hold anywhere for 2x while held. Press and hold the speed button to drop back to normal speed and stay there.\n\nThe CC button appears when a video has subtitles in it, or beside it. If it is not there, Subtitles in the ⋮ menu will go looking — including online, once you have switched that on in Settings. Size, position and everything else about how they look is on the same panel, under Appearance.</string>
    <string name="help_shorts_body">The Shorts tab shows every clip it found. Masonry gives each one its own shape, Grid makes them all the same, and List brings back the names and sizes. Tap one to open the feed on it; everything else follows in a random order.\n\nSwipe up and down to move between clips. There is no gap: the next one is already decoded and waiting.\n\nDrag sideways for brightness on the left half and volume on the right.\n\nDouble tap the left or right side to jump five seconds; double tap the middle to mark a favourite. Tap once to pause.\n\nPress and hold for 2x.\n\nThe padlock locks the screen so a phone in a pocket cannot skip anything.</string>
    <string name="help_library_body">Long press a folder or a video to select it. The toolbar becomes a menu of things you can do to what you picked.\n\nPin anything to keep it at the top, whatever the sort order says.\n\nA locked folder asks for your fingerprint, face or device PIN, shows no preview, and is left out of the shorts feed and out of search.\n\nSearch from the toolbar. In the library it finds videos anywhere, not only folder names.\n\nThe button beside it sets the layout and the order: grid or list, what to sort by, which way round, or no order at all. Each folder keeps its own, so the library can be by name while a camera roll is by date.</string>

